# The scan walks the whole history, so a commit that once held a literal keeps
# reporting even after the file stopped containing it - the fingerprint pins the
# finding to that commit rather than switching the rule off everywhere.
#
# Both are the same thing: a 32-character hex string standing in for a project
# access token in a test. Nothing to rotate; the tokens they imitate are minted
# per project at runtime and never written to the repository. Later commits build
# these fixtures from a repeated character so no new finding is raised.
